<header><h1>The Xxcha Kingdom</h1></header>
<article>
<h2 id="peace-accords"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Peace%20Accords">Peace Accords</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A planet is adjacent to both the system it is in, and every system adjacent to that.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <li>The Xxcha player cannot gain control of a space station with <sc>Peace Accords</sc>, as a space station is not a planet.<sup>2,6</sup></li>
    <li>The Xxcha player may use <sc>Peace Accords</sc> to gain control of a planet in a system that contains another player&rsquo;s ships.<sup>5</sup></li>
    <li>The Xxcha player may use <sc>Peace Accords</sc> to gain control of a planet controlled by another player, if that planet contains no units.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The Xxcha player may use <sc>Peace Accords</sc> to gain control of a planet in another player&rsquo;s home system.<sup>3</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="quash"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Quash">Quash</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><sc>Quash</sc>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Political%20Favor"><i>Political Favor</i></a>, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Political_Secret"><i>Political Secret</i></a> promissory note, and the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Veto"><i>Veto</i></a> action card are all played in the same timing window, before the rider timing window.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If <sc>Quash</sc> is used after any <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Political_Secret"><i>Political Secret</i></a> promissory notes have been played, those will have no effect on the replacement agenda.<sup>1,5</sup></li>
    <li><sc>Quash</sc> may be used on the replacement agenda.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <li><sc>Quash</sc> may be used on a law elected by <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Miscount%20Disclosed"><i>Miscount Disclosed</i></a> when that law is treated as revealed for the revote.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <li>Each agenda is considered separate for the purpose of limiting each pair of players to one transaction per agenda.<sup>5</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="political-favor"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Political%20Favor">Political Favor</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The text of <i>Political Favor</i> is changed to: &ldquo;When an agenda is revealed: Remove 1 token from the Xxcha player&rsquo;s strategy pool and return it to their reinforcements. Then, discard the revealed agenda and reveal 1 agenda from the top of the deck. Players vote on this agenda instead. Then, return this card to the Xxcha player.&rdquo;<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Quash"><sc>Quash</sc></a>, <i>Political Favor</i>, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Political_Secret"><i>Political Secret</i></a> promissory note, and the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Veto"><i>Veto</i></a> action card are all played in the same timing window, before the rider timing window.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the Xxcha player has no command tokens in their strategy pool, <i>Political Favor</i> cannot be played.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="instinct-training"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Instinct%20Training">Instinct Training</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Instinct Training</i> may cancel a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Sabotage"><i>Sabotage</i></a> action card.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player has a second copy of an action card, they may play it if the first was canceled by <i>Instinct Training</i>.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <li>If an action card is canceled by <i>Instinct Training</i>, no costs are paid.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>A player playing an action card announces the following before <i>Instinct Training</i> may be played:<sup>1</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Any targeted planets, system, units, players, cards, outcomes, and/or other such objects.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
        <li>The value of any variable cost to be paid.<sup>5</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Any dice are rolled and any cards are drawn only after all other players have declined to play <i>Instinct Training</i>.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>If an action card instructs a player to research a technology, that player need not announce what technology they are researching until all other players have declined to play <i>Instinct Training</i>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If an action card is played that will have an effect later, such as a rider, that card may only be canceled by <i>Instinct Training</i> when it is originally played.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the action card that was canceled by <i>Instinct Training</i> was to be used to perform a component action, the active player must perform a different action, or pass.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the component action was to be the second action the active player was to perform on their turn, through an effect such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Fleet_Logistics"><i>Fleet Logistics</i></a> technology, the active player may end their turn without performing a second action and without passing.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="nullification-field"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Nullification%20Field">Nullification Field</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Once the Xxcha player resolves the ability of <i>Nullification Field</i>, the active player cannot use any &ldquo;after you activate a system&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>Other players, including the Xxcha player, cannot use any &ldquo;after another player activates a system that&hellip;&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The active player may still use any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4,6</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="loncara-ssodu"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Flagship:~:text=Loncara%20Ssodu">Loncara Ssodu</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>During the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> substep of a tactical action, the active player resolves the <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> abilities of their units first. If the Xxcha player is not the active player, and the <i>Loncara Ssodu</i> is destroyed by another player&rsquo;s space cannon roll, it will not resolve its own <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> ability.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="ggrocuto-rinn"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Ggrocuto%20Rinn">Ggrocuto Rinn</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A planet is adjacent to both the system it is in, and every system adjacent to that.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <li>A planet must be exhausted to be targeted by Ggrocuto Rinn.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <li>Ggrocuto Rinn may ready a planet controlled by another player. If that planet is in a system adjacent to a planet the Xxcha player controls, the infantry removed may belong to another player.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="elder-qanoj"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Elder%20Qanoj">Elder Qanoj</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A planet with zero influence may be used to cast one additional vote.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The Xxcha player may play rider action cards and vote on the same agenda.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The Xxcha player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Political_Secret"><i>Political Secret</i></a> promissory note will not prevent them from voting.<sup>2,14</sup></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player has the Xxcha player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player may vote.<sup>2,14</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="xxekir-grom" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Xxekir%20Grom">Xxekir Grom</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Political%20Data%20Nexus">Political Data Nexus</a> (replaced by &Omega;) <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega; version.<sup>12</sup></li>
    <li>If the Xxcha player draws the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Covert%20Legislation"><i>Covert Legislation</i></a> agenda, they will only draw a hidden agenda if they choose to reveal it. If the Xxcha player is not the speaker, the speaker will view the hidden agenda.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>If the Xxcha player draws, reveals and resolves the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Miscount%20Disclosed"><i>Miscount Disclosed</i></a> agenda, they cast one vote for an outcome of the elected law, and resolve it.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the Xxcha player draws, reveals and resolves the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Public%20Execution"><i>Public Execution</i></a> agenda, the elected player may still vote in the agenda phase following the current action phase.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>When the Xxcha player chooses and reveals an agenda, they may then use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Quash"><sc>Quash</sc></a> ability.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>After the Xxcha player chooses and reveals an agenda, they may play any rider action cards on the revealed agenda.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <li>The Xxcha player chooses the order the two agendas are resolved.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The two agendas are revealed before either is resolved.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>The Xxcha player will resolve all abilities that trigger when or after an agenda is revealed for the first agenda before revealing the second agenda.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>When an agenda outcome with an immediate effect resolves, all players resolve the effect.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>If an agenda would give multiple players a victory point, those players gain that victory point in initiative order, regardless of the Xxcha player&rsquo;s initiative.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Other players may still perform one transaction total with the Xxcha player during this turn, if they are neighbors.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Representative%20Government"><i>Representative Government</i></a> law is in play, it will have no effect on the Xxcha player as they resolve <i>Political Data Nexus</i>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If a third law is put into play, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Agenda_Phase:~:text=Dictate%20Policy"><i>Dictate Policy</i></a> objective cannot be scored until the agenda phase.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Agenda_Phase:~:text=Drive%20the%20Debate"><i>Drive the Debate</i></a> objective cannot be scored while resolving <i>Political Data Nexus</i>.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The effect of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Checks%20and%20Balances"><i>Checks and Balances</i></a> agenda that occurs &ldquo;at the end of this agenda phase&rdquo; is ignored.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Effects from agenda outcomes that occur &ldquo;at the start of the next strategy phase&rdquo; will still occur.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Other players cannot play action cards, including riders, while the Xxcha player resolves <i>Political Data Nexus</i>.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <li>If the Xxcha player draws an agenda that is replaced if there are no laws in play, and there are no laws in play, a new agenda is drawn.<sup>4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="xxekir-grom-2" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Xxekir%20Grom">Xxekir Grom</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Political%20Data%20Nexus">Political Data Nexus &Omega;</a> (replaced by &Omega;&Omega;) <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega;&Omega; version.<sup>7</sup></li>
    <li>During the status phase, public and secret objectives are scored simultaneously. The Xxcha player cannot score a public objective, unlock Xxekir Grom, and then use <i>Political Data Nexus &Omega;</i> in order to score a secret objective, or vice versa.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>The combined value may be spent as either influence or resources, not both.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the Xxcha player owns a planet with three influence and three resources, they cannot score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Amass%20Wealth"><i>Amass Wealth</i></a> objective by exhausting just it and spending three trade goods.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li><i>Political Data Nexus &Omega;</i> does not change the value used by abilities that reference a planet&rsquo;s resource value; the printed resource value of the planet is used.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>A space dock will not add the influence value of the planet it is on to its <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> value.<sup>2</sup></li>
        <li>The resource values of the planets the Xxcha player controls will not contribute to unlocking <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Elder%20Qanoj">Elder Qanoj</a>.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li><i>Political Data Nexus &Omega;</i> does not apply when scoring the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_4:~:text=Establish%20Hegemony"><i>Establish Hegemony</i></a> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_4:~:text=Hoard%20Raw%20Materials"><i>Hoard Raw Materials</i></a> objectives.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The resource value of a planet will be added to its influence value when the Xxcha player casts votes during the agenda phase.<sup>12</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="xxekir-grom-3"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Xxekir%20Grom">Xxekir Grom</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Planetary%20Defense%20Nexus">Planetary Defense Nexus &Omega;&Omega;</a><sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The units may be placed on a readied planet.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Multiple units may be placed on the same planet.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="indomitus"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Mech:~:text=Indomitus">Indomitus</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>During the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> substep of a tactical action, the active player resolves the <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> abilities of their units first. If the Xxcha player is not the active player, and their ships are removed by another player&rsquo;s space cannon roll, they must immediately remove units to meet their capacity limit. They will not resolve the <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> abilities of any of their removed mechs.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>An Indomitus being transported in the space area of a system may still use its <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> ability.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="archons-gift"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Breakthrough:~:text=Archon%27s%20Gift">Archon&rsquo;s Gift</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A source of both influence and resources, such as a planet, may be spent for one or the other, but not both.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>For example, Archon Tau will provide one resource or one influence, not two.<sup>2</sup></li>
        <li>For example, if the Xxcha player wishes to score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Amass%20Wealth"><i>Amass Wealth</i></a> objective, each planet they exhaust will contribute to either the resource requirement or the influence requirement, but cannot partially contribute to both.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li><i>Archon&rsquo;s Gift</i> only changes how a planet&rsquo;s influence and resources may be spent. It does not change the value for any other game effect.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>A space dock cannot use the influence value of the planet it is on to calculate its <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> value.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>The influence value of a planet will not increase the number of units the Xxcha player may produce when using the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Integrated_Economy"><i>Integrated Economy</i></a> technology.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>The resource values of the planets the Xxcha player controls will not contribute to unlocking <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Leaders:~:text=Elder%20Qanoj">Elder Qanoj</a>.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li><i>Archon&rsquo;s Gift</i> does not apply when scoring the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_4:~:text=Establish%20Hegemony"><i>Establish Hegemony</i></a> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_4:~:text=Hoard%20Raw%20Materials"><i>Hoard Raw Materials</i></a> objectives.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>The Xxcha player cannot use the influence value of a planet when they gain trade goods with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Mining%20Initiative"><i>Mining Initiative</i></a> action card. Other players cannot use the influence value when they gain trade goods from the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Uprising"><i>Uprising</i></a> action card if they choose to exhaust one of the Xxcha player&rsquo;s planets.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>
</article>
